ok 6 - restore-chain manifest carries the ordered bounded plan edges and a unique hash
ok 7 - restore-chain manifest is private with forced RLS and no browser grants
ok 8 - cms_restore_revision exists as the worker-only restore command
ok 9 - a same-schema restore returns a new draft revision
ok 10 - a zero-edge restore records a manifest with no plan edges
true
ok 11 - a multi-edge restore translates content across every recorded plan
ok 12 - a multi-edge manifest records consecutive bounded edges and a recomputed hash
ok 13 - a chain that no longer matches the derived path is refused, never guessed
ok 14 - a restore chain longer than 64 edges is refused, never truncated
ok 15 - no over-limit restore manifest is ever recorded
ok 16 - a field without a registered transform is a typed restore refusal
ok 17 - a required target field without a literal default refuses rather than inventing one
ok 18 - an incompatible template resolution is a typed restore refusal
ok 19 - a replayed restore key returns the original revision without duplicate effects
ok 20 - a stale entry version fails the restore CAS with the typed VERSION_MISMATCH path (P0001, as append and resolve; cascade: write-path audit P2-S10-AC-025, was SQLSTATE 40001)
ok 21 - a restored draft records its current-draft and source parent chain
ok 22 - the source revision stays an immutable draft snapshot after restore
ok 23 - restore audit/outbox evidence records only chain identity and safe counts
ok
